---
/**
 * Plausible Analytics — tracker script for a page.
 *
 * Renders nothing when analytics are disabled (staging, the flag is
 * off, or the script URL is missing). When enabled it emits
 * Plausible's current two-script installation snippet.
 *
 * ## Why two script tags
 *
 * Plausible's per-site script (`https://<instance>/js/pa-<id>.js`)
 * is self-contained: it has the reporting domain and the event
 * endpoint baked in, and it does not read a `data-domain` or
 * `data-api` attribute. The legacy `js/script.js` did read those
 * attributes, which is why older integrations carried a
 * `data-domain="..."` attribute.
 *
 * The per-site script also does not self-initialise reliably on its
 * own — it guards its initialiser with `if (window.plausible &&
 * window.plausible.l)`. Without the bootstrap below, `window.plausible`
 * stays a bare stub with no `l` flag and no event listeners, so the
 * script loads but never sends a pageview. The bootstrap defines the
 * queue stub, sets `plausible.o`, and calls `plausible.init()`.
 *
 * ## Why `is:inline` on both tags
 *
 * - The inline bootstrap: without `is:inline`, Astro treats the tag as
 *   a module, rewrites it to `<script type="module">`, and defers it.
 *   A deferred module runs after parsing, which is too late to define
 *   the `window.plausible` stub before the async tracker executes.
 *   `is:inline` keeps it a classic synchronous script, byte-for-byte.
 * - The external tracker: `is:inline` is the documented way to load a
 *   remote script without Astro trying to bundle or resolve it.
 *
 * ## Script ordering
 *
 * The tracker is `async`, so it may run before or after the
 * bootstrap. Both orders are safe: the tracker replays anything
 * queued on `window.plausible.q`, and the bootstrap sets
 * `plausible.o` before calling `init()`. Whichever runs first, the
 * script initialises exactly once.
 *
 * The three guards (opt-in flag, staging exclusion, URL present) are
 * applied in `src/lib/plausible.ts` — see `getPlausibleConfig`.
 */

import { getPlausibleConfig } from '@/lib/plausible';

const { enabled, scriptUrl } = getPlausibleConfig(Astro.site);
---

{enabled && (
  <>
    <!-- Privacy-friendly analytics by Plausible -->
    <script async is:inline src={scriptUrl}></script>
    <script is:inline>
      window.plausible=window.plausible||function(){(plausible.q=plausible.q||[]).push(arguments)},plausible.init=plausible.init||function(i){plausible.o=i||{}};
      plausible.init()
    </script>
  </>
)}
